Allow DSV41_FAST_LOAD=1 as an explicit opt-in.

The stock dsv41-native-prepare mod treats the stock weight loader as a policy
requirement and rejects any lane with DSV41_FAST_LOAD=1. The same adapter set
already boots with the fast loader (knapcio-baseline-diag does it), so this is a
policy guard, not a dependency. The patch keeps the default behaviour (stock
loader) and adds DSV41_PREPARE_ALLOW_FAST_LOAD=1 as the opt-in.

Apply from the dsv41-native-prepare directory:
    patch -p1 < prepare-allow-fast-load.patch

--- a/prepare.py
+++ b/prepare.py
@@ -98,9 +98,15 @@
         env.get("SERVER_PORT") == env.get("SPARKRUN_PORT"),
         "SERVER_PORT must match the serving port",
     )
+    # The stock loader is a policy choice, not a requirement of this lane: the
+    # fast loader is gated in the image (adapter/fast_load.py) and the same
+    # adapter set boots with it (knapcio-baseline-diag). Opt in explicitly so
+    # the default lane keeps its ~220 s/boot stock behaviour.
     require(
-        env.get("DSV41_FAST_LOAD", "0") == "0",
-        "this experimental baseline requires DSV41_FAST_LOAD=0",
+        env.get("DSV41_FAST_LOAD", "0") == "0"
+        or env.get("DSV41_PREPARE_ALLOW_FAST_LOAD", "0") == "1",
+        "this experimental baseline requires DSV41_FAST_LOAD=0 "
+        "(set DSV41_PREPARE_ALLOW_FAST_LOAD=1 to opt this lane into the fast loader)",
     )
     require(
         env.get("PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF") == "expandable_segments:False",
